 "short_circuit_method": "INVx1, 2 fF load, driven by an ideal edge of the stated 0-100% length. The capacitive part of the rail energy does not depend on the input edge, so the rise above the fastest edge's value is the short-circuit (both-devices-on) energy. The curve is U-shaped at 0.7 V: fast edges cost extra through gate-drain (Miller) coupling, slow edges through short circuit, so the excess is quoted over the CHEAPEST edge, not the fastest."
}